## std/sync/atomic/atomic_int — AtomicInt canonical constructor (D.10 Phase 2)
##
## AtomicInt is a built-in type (`TYPE_ATOMIC`); the typechecker recognizes
## it as an annotation thanks to the AtomicInt branch in
## `typecheck.qz::tc_parse_type` and the reverse mapping in `tc_type_name`.
## The mutating intrinsics (`atomic_load` / `atomic_store` / `atomic_add` /
## `atomic_sub` / `atomic_exchange` / `atomic_xor` / `atomic_cas`) are
## already wired through the TYPE_ATOMIC UFCS branch in
## `typecheck_expr_handlers.qz` — `a.load()` desugars to `atomic_load(a)`,
## etc. This file just adds the canonical `AtomicInt.new(initial)` static
## constructor so atomic counters can be constructed in the same idiom as
## the rest of the D.10 toolkit (`Channel.new(64)`, `Mutex.new(0)`,
## `Spinlock.new()`, `RwLock.new(0)`).
##
## Usage:
##
##   var counter = AtomicInt.new(0)
##   counter.add(1)
##   var snapshot = counter.load()
##   if counter.cas(snapshot, snapshot + 10)
##     # ...
##   end
##
## Legacy `atomic_new(initial)` remains callable during the migration
## window. Both expressions produce a `TYPE_ATOMIC` value.

extend AtomicInt
  ## Construct a new atomic integer initialized to `initial`. Canonical
  ## D.10 surface; equivalent to the legacy free function `atomic_new`.
  def new(initial: Int): AtomicInt = atomic_new(initial)
end
